course: dictionary
lesson: 13027
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Bank» can be the side of a river or a place to keep money. To pick the right meaning, read the words around the word and ask what would make sense there.
explain: The word «faculty» has four main meanings. It can be a natural ability of the body or mind, such as hearing. It can be a group of departments in a university. In American schools, it can mean all the teachers. It can also mean a special talent for something.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. «Owls have a keen faculty of hearing» is about a natural ability, because hearing is something the body can do. «The faculty voted on the new timetable» is about teachers, because a school timetable is their work.
fact: A faculty can be a natural ability of the body or mind, such as sight, hearing or memory.
fact: A faculty can be a group of departments in a university, such as the Faculty of Science.
fact: In American schools, «the faculty» means all the teachers of a school or university.
fact: A faculty can also be a special skill or talent, as in «a faculty for languages».
exercise: «Owls have a keen faculty of hearing.» What does faculty mean here? | A kind of bird | *A natural ability of the body or mind | A group of departments in a university | All the teachers of a school
exercise: «The faculty voted to change the school timetable.» What does faculty mean here? | A special talent | *All the teachers of the school | A natural ability | A group of university departments
exercise: «Maya has a faculty for drawing, and she sketches every day.» What does faculty for mean here? | A part of the brain | A room where paintings are kept | A group of artists in a university | *A special skill or talent for something
test: «After the accident, Grandma was still in full possession of her faculties.» What does faculties mean here? | She was fast asleep | She had lost her voice | *Her mind still worked well | She could not walk
test: «My cousin studies in the Faculty of Science at university.» What is a faculty here? | A type of science lab | *A group of departments in a university | A natural ability | All the students in the school
exam: «Zara has a faculty for languages, and she learns new words in a week.» What does faculty for mean here? | *A special talent for something | Part of the ear | A university building | A group of teachers
